From: awesoMux Linux <noreply@awesomux.local>
Subject: [PATCH] embedded: retain terminal core across Linux GL remounts

Purpose: Keep shell, job, and scrollback while GTK reparents a pane.
Upstream pin: f2d5758f6305867dc36b36293c6165d8152b853e
Files: include/ghostty.h, src/Surface.zig, src/apprt/embedded.zig, src/renderer/{OpenGL,generic,image}.zig, src/renderer/opengl/shaders.zig
Wrapper limitation: renderer display lifecycle is not in the embedded C API.
Coverage: live PID survival, output, focus, detached close, repeated remount, and one-shot GL fault integration.
Rebase risk: renderer lifecycle, image/shader CPU ownership, or embedded Surface teardown changes.

diff --git a/include/ghostty.h b/include/ghostty.h
--- a/include/ghostty.h
+++ b/include/ghostty.h
@@ -1185,6 +1185,13 @@
 GHOSTTY_API bool ghostty_surface_process_exited(ghostty_surface_t);
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_refresh(ghostty_surface_t);
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_draw(ghostty_surface_t);
+#ifdef __linux__
+/* Release and restore display resources without ending the terminal process. */
+GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_display_unrealized(ghostty_surface_t);
+GHOSTTY_API bool ghostty_surface_display_realized(ghostty_surface_t);
+/* Final teardown when the original GL context cannot be made current. */
+GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_free_display_lost(ghostty_surface_t);
+#endif
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_set_content_scale(ghostty_surface_t, double, double);
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_set_focus(ghostty_surface_t, bool);
 GHOSTTY_API void ghostty_surface_set_occlusion(ghostty_surface_t, bool);
